\title{deribit: API Wrapper to the Deribit Crypto Derivatives Exchange}
\description{
A connector for the public market-data surface of the Deribit crypto
options and derivatives exchange (\code{deribit.com}), built on the shared
\link[connectcore:RestClient]{connectcore::RestClient} transport base. It speaks Deribit's JSON-RPC 2.0
over HTTP GET (the \verb{public/*} methods, which need no API key) and returns
tidy \link[data.table:data.table]{data.table::data.table}s.
}
\details{
\subsection{What is covered in this version}{

Phase 1 is \strong{public market data only} (no trading, no authenticated
surface). \link{DeribitMarketData} covers the instrument universe
(\code{get_instruments}, \code{get_currencies}), live quotes (\code{get_ticker},
\code{get_order_book}, \code{get_index_price}), the DVOL volatility index
(\code{get_volatility_index_data}), perpetual funding (\code{get_funding_rate_history},
\code{get_funding_rate_value}), public trades (\code{get_last_trades_by_instrument}),
and the option-chain book summaries (\code{get_book_summary_by_currency},
\code{get_book_summary_by_instrument}, \code{get_option_chain}).
}

\subsection{Sync and async}{

Every request-making surface supports both a synchronous mode (returns a
\code{data.table}) and an asynchronous mode (returns a \link[promises:promise]{promises::promise}
resolving to the same \code{data.table}), selected by the \code{async} argument at
construction. There is a single sync/async branch point, inherited from
\code{connectcore}. See \link{DeribitMarketData} for the shared mechanism.
}

\subsection{No API key}{

The \verb{public/*} endpoints this package wraps require no credential, so a
\code{DeribitMarketData} client is constructed with no key. The private trading
surface (orders, positions, account) is deliberately out of scope for this
phase.
}

\subsection{Typed errors}{

Every failure is a classed condition — \link{deribit_conditions}: a Deribit
JSON-RPC error surfaces as a \code{deribit_api_error} layered onto the shared
\code{connectcore_api_error} chain (carrying the HTTP \code{status}, the JSON-RPC
\code{code}, and the \code{reason}/\code{param} detail), and an input-validation failure
surfaces as \code{deribit_validation_error} under the \code{deribit_error} domain root.
}
